<p>After much deliberation, I've changed my mind. This is getting my downvote.</p>
<p>The problem I have with this, is that it blurs the line between being Safe and being Thaumiel, much like a Keter and an Apollyon<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-576531-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-576531-1')">1</a></sup>, but not in a good way.</p>
<p>The only reason why I hesitated and didn't give this a downvote was because the writing was good. That was a mistake.</p>
<p>My issue with this is it setting this precedent that, there are going to be scips that should be classified as Safe yet, they're classified as Thaumiel and renders the entire point of having a Safe class around, null.</p>
